cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VisionForge in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "VisionForge: a local-first computer-vision experimentation platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Reis"
    given-names: "Marcus Vinícius"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcus-vreis/VisionForge"
url: "https://github.com/marcus-vreis/VisionForge"
license: MIT
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-07-02
keywords:
  - computer-vision
  - deep-learning
  - pytorch
  - experiment-tracking
  - reproducibility
  - image-classification
  - object-detection
  - semantic-segmentation
  - anomaly-detection
abstract: >-
  VisionForge is a local-first platform for training, validating and comparing
  computer-vision models on the researcher's own GPU. It covers five task
  families (classification, object detection, image regression, semantic
  segmentation and anomaly detection) behind one canonical interface, and
  treats statistical rigor as a first-class feature: multi-seed replicates
  with 95% confidence intervals, K-fold cross-validation, hyperparameter
  sweeps (grid/random/Optuna), and full run provenance (config, seeds,
  library versions, CUDA/cuDNN/GPU) recorded in a versioned run.json contract.
